    {
      "stableId": "math2-1997-q16",
      "sourceYear": 1997,
      "subjectCode": "math2",
      "type": "solution",
      "questionNumber": 16,
      "stem": "已知函数 f (x ) 连续，且 $\\operatorname* { l i m } _ { x \\to 0 } { \\frac { f ( x ) } { x } } = 2$ ，设 $\\varphi ( x ) = \\int _ { 0 } ^ { 1 } f ( x t ) \\mathrm { d } t$ ，求 $\\varphi ^ { \\prime } ( x )$ 并讨论$\\varphi ^ { \\prime } ( x )$ 在 x 0处的连续性",
      "options": [],
      "answer": null,
      "answerStatus": "missing",
      "explanation": "解. 由题设 $\\operatorname* { l i m } _ { x \\to 0 } { \\frac { f ( x ) } { x } } = 2$ 知 $f ( 0 ) = 0 , f ^ { \\prime } ( 0 ) = 2$ ，且有 $\\varphi ( 0 ) = 0$ ．当 $x \\neq 0$ 时有\n\n$$\n\\varphi (x) = \\int_ {0} ^ {1} f (x t) \\mathrm{d} t = \\frac {\\int_ {0} ^ {x} f (u) \\mathrm{d} u}{x} \\Rightarrow \\varphi^ {\\prime} (x) = \\frac {x f (x) - \\int_ {0} ^ {x} f (u) \\mathrm{d} u}{x ^ {2}},\n$$\n\n当 $x = 0$ 时有\n\n$$\n\\varphi^ {\\prime} (0) = \\lim _ {x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac {\\varphi (x) - \\varphi (0)}{x} = \\lim _ {x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac {\\int_ {0} ^ {x} f (u) \\mathrm{d} u}{x ^ {2}} = \\lim _ {x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac {f (x)}{2 x} = 1.\n$$\n\n从而\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} \\lim _ {x \\rightarrow 0} \\varphi^ {\\prime} (x) = \\lim _ {x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac {x f (x) - \\int_ {0} ^ {x} f (u) \\mathrm{d} u}{x ^ {2}} = \\lim _ {x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac {f (x)}{x} - \\lim _ {x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac {\\int_ {0} ^ {x} f (u) \\mathrm{d} u}{x ^ {2}} \\\\ = 2 - 1 = 1 = \\varphi^ {\\prime} (0), \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$\n\n即 $\\varphi ^ { \\prime } ( x )$ 在 x = 0 处连续",
      "explanationStatus": "sourced_from_aggregate",
      "reviewStatus": "needs_human_review",
      "finalizationStatus": "blocked",
